      "writtenOn": "2022-08-16T21:28:09Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "For ambiguous matches where two costs are the same, SkSL has always preferred the first overload that matches. This matters a lot for calls with Literals, like:\n```\n  $genType  min($genType  x, $genType  y);\n  $genHType min($genHType x, $genHType y);\n  $genIType min($genIType x, $genIType y);\n  \n  float x \u003d min(4, 5);   // we want $genType, not $genIType\n```\nAn UnresolvedFunction node held the overloads in order, from top to bottom. Walking the FunctionDeclaration overload chain linked-list goes \"backwards,\" from bottom to top. Because we are walking the list in backwards order, this affected which overload would \"win\" in cases of a tie.\n\nThis is actually the root cause of skbug.com/8791 (I commented on it when I discovered this).",
      "parentUuid": "90d3640d_2be724a4",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 874,
        "startChar": 17,
        "endLine": 874,
